AUDIO: 'There are VPNs that you can use when you\'re browsing the internet. Again, this is not a silver bullet. What does a VPN do? The VPN is a middleman.'

[35:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If I just go online and go visit a website, I have Verizon for my cell phone service when I use my iPhone. I have a different service for my other phone.'

[36:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But, if I go visit a website from my iPhone, my data goes from my phone to Verizon to the website that I\'m visiting. Verizon sees everything that I do'

[36:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'online. And the website can see my IP address and they can tie that back to oh, you were on this site before, you you\'re going to this site after. So, the website I\'m visiting gets my IP address'

[36:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and my uh internet service provider can see everything that I\'m doing. The VPN is a middleman. What happens is my data is encrypted, it'

[36:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'goes through a VPN. What Verizon sees is I connected to a VPN. They have no idea what what happens to the data after that. So, all they see is it went to a VPN.'

[36:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The VPN then goes to the website that I\'m visiting. What does that website see? Oh, I\'m coming from a VPN. It prevents the website I\'m visiting from getting my IP address and it'

[37:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prevents my internet service provider from seeing the website that I\'m going to. So, as a middleman, it it disrupts that flow of information to give me more privacy. That also means it\'s extremely important'

[37:24] [scene:presentation]
VISUAL: Dr. Jon Padfield speaking, holding a notebook.
AUDIO: 'that I pick a reputable VPN because the VPN has both both sides of the equation. And so, when you go out online right now, there are so many VPNs out there and most of them I do not trust.'

